# local.properties — build configuration template
#
# Copy this file to `local.properties` (which is gitignored and never committed)
# and fill in what you need. Everything here is optional: without any of it the
# project still builds, still runs the full unit-test suite, and still runs the
# app — Dropbox sync is the only feature that needs configuration.
#
#     cp local.properties.example local.properties
#
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Required for the build
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Where your Android SDK is. The Android Studio wizard writes this automatically,
# so you only need it for a command-line build. Windows: escape the backslashes.
#
# sdk.dir=C\:\\Users\\you\\AppData\\Local\\Android\\Sdk
#
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional: Dropbox sync
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The app keys are a public PKCE client_id, not a secret in the usual sense — but
# they name a real app in a real Dropbox console, so they belong to whoever
# builds the app rather than being written into the source.
#
# Without a key the build still compiles; the app asks for the key in Settings.
#
# To enable sync, create your own app at https://www.dropbox.com/developers/apps
# (Scoped access, App folder), register the redirect URI shown under Settings —
# `questa://oauth` for a release build, `questa-dev://oauth` for the `.dev`
# debug build — then either enter the key in the app, or:
#
# optional: seeds your own install once; the app asks for the key otherwise
# dropboxAppKey=<your app key>
#
# The environment variable DROPBOX_APP_KEY overrides this.
#
# The key is written into the app once, on first start, when no key is stored.
# After that only the key in Settings counts. To build an APK without it, run
# `build.bat release nokey` (or Gradle with -PnoKeySeed).
#
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional: development-only account safety
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# REAL_ACCOUNT_UNLOCKED defaults to false and blocks all real Dropbox traffic.
# Set it to true only on a machine you control, when you intend to sync a real
# account. Do not ship it enabled.
#
# realAccountUnlocked=false
#
# Comma-separated account ids excluded from the interlock's refuse-list.
#
# scratchAccountIds=
#
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Tests
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Unit tests need sdk.dir (or ANDROID_HOME). They never use your Dropbox key:
# the test app always starts with no key and sets its own fake test key, and
# the tests talk to a fake Dropbox server, never the real one. Keep
# realAccountUnlocked unset (false) when you run the tests.
